; A helper parameter has ONE identity (backlog-158). hf_params gave each param
; its POSITIONAL index as var_id while every use site carried the typer's id, and
; the interpreter resolves by id before name — so with a module constant ahead of
; the helper (which puts the ids inside the 1 <= c <= n-1 failure window) every
; reference was off by one.
;
; MUST be its own file: the typer's id counter is global and persists across
; kernels, so a probe placed after other kernels falls outside the window and
; passes with and without the fix. That is exactly why the previous probe
