 (preprocess
  (pps sarek_ppx))
 (flags
  (:standard -w -32-33-34-69)))

; LD_LIBRARY_PATH is set so the ZLUDA CUDA/PTX driver is reachable and the
; CUDA/PTX legs of this test RUN in the default gate.
;
; They did not. The test's header states that CUDA/PTX compiles BOTH nested
; kernels and lands the store at both levels, "measured under ZLUDA" on two
; devices, and [predict_struct_gap]'s reason for keeping CUDA/PTX OFF the
; tolerated-failure allowlist rests on that same measurement. Nothing put ZLUDA
; on the loader path, so a plain `dune runtest` enumerated 7 devices, printed
; ZERO CUDA/PTX rows and exited 0: the gate could not reproduce either claim.
; Two changes close it — the test now prints a named NOT-MEASURED-HERE line for
; any framework its header claims and the run did not enumerate (so a silent
; drop is impossible even where this rule finds nothing), and this rule makes
; the device present where it exists.
;
; $HOME/opt/zluda is the location the rules further up already document as this
; project's ZLUDA checkout. Trade-offs, stated rather than assumed:
;   - a machine WITHOUT ZLUDA: the loader ignores a nonexistent directory, so
;     the rule is a no-op and the test prints its NOT-MEASURED-HERE line. No new
;     failure.
;   - a machine with a NATIVE CUDA driver: libcuda.so.1 is on the default loader
;     path, so replacing LD_LIBRARY_PATH does not hide it. A host that reaches
;     its CUDA driver ONLY through an inherited LD_LIBRARY_PATH loses the PTX
;     leg here — and gets the loud named line, not a false green.
; Same precedent as the RUSTICL_FEATURES=fp64 rule above: set the variable that
; makes a leg actually exercised, rather than documenting it in a comment and
; letting the leg quietly not run.

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (action
  (setenv
   LD_LIBRARY_PATH
   %{env:HOME=}/opt/zluda
   (run %{dep:test_record_field_store.exe}))))

